ns managing patients on anticoagulants or with underlying kidney disease. [Data: Relationships (1658, 1659)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"盐酸美他环素 shows limited but notable pharmacological interactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While less central than 多西环素, 盐酸美他环素 (methacycline hydrochloride) is present in the community with specific effects on diagnostic indicators. It elevates measured levels of 碱性磷酸酶 (alkaline phosphatase) and 血清淀粉酶 (serum amylase), which could lead to misinterpretation of liver or pancreatic function tests if not accounted for. These interactions highlight the need for awareness among clinicians when evaluating lab results in patients receiving tetracycline derivatives. [Data: Entities (7303); Relationships (3590, 3597)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug–drug interaction risks extend beyond direct adverse effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond its primary indications and side effects, 多西环素 exhibits clinically relevant drug–drug interactions (DDIs). For example, concurrent use with barbiturates, phenytoin, or carbamazepine may reduce its plasma concentration due to enzyme induction. Conversely, co-administration with isotretinoin increases the risk of pseudotumor cerebri. Additionally, although not directly linked in the provided relationships, general tetracycline-class warnings include reduced absorption when taken with metal ion–containing medications (e.g., calcium, magnesium, iron), as seen with 土霉素 (oxytetracycline) interacting with 金属离子药物. This suggests similar precautions likely apply to 多西环素 despite absence of explicit records. [Data: Relationships (10852, 33838)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderately high due to 多西环素's role in treating high-consequence infectious diseases and its potential for serious adverse reactions and drug interactions that affect patient safety and clinical decision-making.